\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Why is the following optimization problem NP-hard: given a directed graph D=(V,A), a root r, and a cost vector c\textasciicircum{}v for each v\textbackslash{}ne r, find an arborescence T minimizing the sum over v\textbackslash{}ne r of c\textasciicircum{}v(P\textasciicircum{}v), where P\textasciicircum{}v is the r-to-v path in T? \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2018/50}{[S2]}
